<h2 class="sec-title" style="max-width:840px">Reliability and performance, carried from <span>silicon</span> to the <span>racetrack</span>.</h2>
</div>
<div class="about__grid">
<div>
<p class="reveal about__lead" data-reveal-delay="80">I'm a Software &amp; AI engineer with 3+ years building production data pipelines, ML systems, and backend tooling — grounded in the reliability and performance discipline of low-level hardware engineering.</p>
<p class="reveal about__p" data-reveal-delay="160">At Intel I spent three years deep in AI-accelerator silicon, building C/C++ and Python tooling across 9+ FPGA and NPU programs, deploying Kubernetes-hosted dashboards, and automating the validation that kept engineering teams moving fast and correct under real load.</p>
<p class="reveal about__p" data-reveal-delay="240">Today I design, train, and deploy ML models against real-time data. At FYM Technologies I architect end-to-end telemetry pipelines for professional racing teams — turning raw sensor streams into live strategy and performance predictions.</p>
</div>
